## **Clarified Imagery**\
\
Ah, now I see the picture! Here's a version that captures the ground-level trucks tipping down into the basement shopping space:\
\
```\
"Floormarts are just open basement pits with tin roofs. The shop floor is below ground level, and trucks just back up to the edge and tip their loads straight down into the store. No walls, no barriers\'97they can dump anywhere: kitchen goods over there, clothing over here, food wherever. Everything just tumbles down from street level and piles up on the basement floor. It's a shopper's problem to dodge the avalanche when deliveries arrive. I was once digging through the dry food section looking for fusilli and found a body at the bottom of a pasta mountain\'97probably got caught in the cascade when the Barilla truck tipped its load. Whatever you do, don't go near a Floormart."\
```\
\
**Key imagery:**\
- "basement pits" - emphasizes being below ground\
- "trucks just back up to the edge and tip their loads straight down" - clear vertical dumping\
- "tumbles down from street level" - shows the falling merchandise\
- "dodge the avalanche" - captures the danger of being below\
- "caught in the cascade" - explains how someone gets buried\
